#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059375 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "979859e4-b60c-548d-8da6-b180400e1b07" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "14e05d4f-373c-5d1f-aa59-7ee52466480e" :question/math-academy-id "e-14762" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12 & 1\\end{aligned}$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =0|\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ -12 & 1\\end{aligned}|-(-3)|\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}|+6|\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0(8+96)+3(8+48)+6(-96+48) \\\\  & =0+3\\cdot 56+6\\cdot (-48) \\\\  & =168-288 \\\\  & =-120\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059376 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/id #uuid "d7516cec-bd96-59db-98cd-5d82e41fa719" :question/math-academy-id "e-14763" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $A$ given below?\n\n- $\\det(A) = 0$\n\n- $A$ is **not** a singular matrix\n\n- $A$ is a singular matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 7\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(0-4)-2(7-3)+3(4-0) \\\\  & =-4-2\\cdot 4+3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-4-8+12 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\det(A)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059377 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant"}] :question/id #uuid "7780340c-43d6-5d38-9270-865914098218" :question/math-academy-id "e-14764" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of  $[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ k & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ is $2,$ find the value of the constant $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ k & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =3|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}k & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(12-10)-1(3k-0)+2(2k-0) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 3k+2\\cdot 2k \\\\  & =6-3k+4k \\\\  & =k+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $2,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k+6 & =2 \\\\ k & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303307 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a191dba-16dd-5b91-b92c-74456c9286df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303309} {:answer/id #uuid "b5b00579-93ef-5741-b329-98cc98e20e8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303310} {:answer/id #uuid "e0e1a3d4-3256-56a2-8579-d0cb7725057f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303311} {:answer/id #uuid "d91db950-9a7f-5572-9414-c66c3ae0f4a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303312} {:answer/id #uuid "8dac9c91-67ef-5130-939b-a0b625916607" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a191dba-16dd-5b91-b92c-74456c9286df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303309} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d5536c7-7d93-5b6f-bcb0-08074eb5662e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1de7b7b6-d74a-53dc-9249-a5265a42e232" :question/math-academy-id "q-128476" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $T$ given below?\n\n- $T$ is a singular matrix\n- $T$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- $det(T)=-30$\n\n \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(1-3)-3(2-1)-5(6-1) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-2-3-25 \\\\  & =-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(T)=-30\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements II and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320311 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5864ebc-bd7f-518a-ae9b-cfcd1031f011" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320313} {:answer/id #uuid "e053aafa-15e9-53d8-b693-05a611f29ea3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $8$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320314} {:answer/id #uuid "8d870840-8390-59b1-9bf4-6f4cc2c09cf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-5$ and $1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320315} {:answer/id #uuid "308cd1c5-fdc4-50d9-a9ee-e91c144ed145" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320316} {:answer/id #uuid "d6454265-e507-5721-bd63-f7e365b93e7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-6$ and $3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e053aafa-15e9-53d8-b693-05a611f29ea3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $8$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320314} :answer-field/id #uuid "653b22c2-ac63-55f3-b4fb-7b1a85208b53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320312}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "30a80f14-b653-5ec9-a12d-20d43bb40f91" :question/math-academy-id "q-128506" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & m \\\\ m & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nis $-29$, find all the possible values of $m.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $m:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & m \\\\ m & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-6|\\begin{aligned}m & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+m|\\begin{aligned}m & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3-0)-6(m-0)+m(m-6) \\\\  & =3-6m+{m}^{2}-6m \\\\  & ={m}^{2}-12m+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-29,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}-12m+3 & =-29 \\\\ {m}^{2}-12m+32 & =0 \\\\ m & =\\frac{-(-12)\\pm \\sqrt{{12}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 32}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pm \\sqrt{16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pm 4}{2} \\\\  & =6\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $m=4$ and $m=8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303321 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20471aec-848e-513e-968a-d6aec97caa96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303323} {:answer/id #uuid "b476adf8-40ae-54da-ac98-df291a8dd1ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{5}{3}$ and $1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303324} {:answer/id #uuid "09c5767d-a3b0-5d1a-860a-026fafd6510c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303325} {:answer/id #uuid "f5001a26-00b9-5b68-b868-a2749147bd0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{5}{3}$ and $-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303326} {:answer/id #uuid "e19af8f1-f3a5-5db5-ac86-072cb48385c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e19af8f1-f3a5-5db5-ac86-072cb48385c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303327} :answer-field/id #uuid "59e39d2d-4575-5e43-a400-caa5668def86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "01aa8d57-113b-5436-b1ef-e962e4723b9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-18256" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of \n$[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3y & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & y & -5\\end{aligned}]$\n is $81,$ find all the possible values of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3y & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & y & -5\\end{aligned}| & =4|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ y & -5\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}-3y & 1 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}-3y & -2 \\\\ 2 & y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot (10-y)-2\\cdot (15y-2)+3\\cdot (-3{y}^{2}+4) \\\\  & =40-4y-30y+4-9{y}^{2}+12 \\\\  & =-9{y}^{2}-34y+56\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $81,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9{y}^{2}-34y+56 & =81 \\\\ -9{y}^{2}-34y-25 & =0 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}+34y+25 & =0 \\\\ y & =\\frac{-34\\pm \\sqrt{{34}^{2}-4\\cdot 9\\cdot 25}}{2\\cdot 9} \\\\  & =\\frac{-34\\pm \\sqrt{256}}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{-34\\pm 16}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{-17\\pm 8}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $y=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303339 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "979859e4-b60c-548d-8da6-b180400e1b07" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ff34e01-249d-5f34-a6ee-d7b6e18a50c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303341} {:answer/id #uuid "d14d2afd-862f-529e-bfcf-55965bdfb7a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d14d2afd-862f-529e-bfcf-55965bdfb7a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303342} :answer-field/id #uuid "18824b8b-d559-5060-91df-b38c33b99b4d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303340}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "711f7b0f-8038-59ce-9d0e-6b423dd7512d" :question/math-academy-id "q-280390" :question/problem "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],$ then $det(A)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| & =0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|+(-3)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-2(0-0)-3(0-0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303343 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "979859e4-b60c-548d-8da6-b180400e1b07" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a865554-0a16-5080-a9ac-454763f1b02a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303345} {:answer/id #uuid "70a3288c-9a8b-5258-a31a-e86f7929ead4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303346} {:answer/id #uuid "3cf721f7-87c3-51fa-aaf3-91839fc65583" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303347} {:answer/id #uuid "31b4cba5-feaf-5b8a-a451-d244cad17919" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303348} {:answer/id #uuid "5edc7390-a20c-5673-9b84-c60171d426fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3cf721f7-87c3-51fa-aaf3-91839fc65583" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303347} :answer-field/id #uuid "216ec6d2-dd2c-5323-ac0f-4bb01f046b29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303344}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4620a567-cdc4-53d7-9a4f-ea734b82495f" :question/math-academy-id "q-38100" :question/problem "Find the value of $|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}|.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(32-0)+1(0-0)+2(0-0) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 32 \\\\  & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303350 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9def4b4a-1dd6-546f-a05a-5cec780136ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303352} {:answer/id #uuid "ea8d1bfd-dd9d-5df0-bb07-aecfb19ecda9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303353} {:answer/id #uuid "e3c5ada5-b582-58a4-9b16-63c359d07add" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303354} {:answer/id #uuid "19695a11-6184-50a6-b7e4-a8ce98068372" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303355} {:answer/id #uuid "7e56084e-c049-5d03-8053-7d8f8a131ad4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9def4b4a-1dd6-546f-a05a-5cec780136ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303352} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5ffcb6e-0917-5f6f-a0aa-f5850879ca37" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303351}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f488e99f-6a91-5199-9a3f-4686ca4250e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-77477" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $S$ given below?\n\n- $S$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- $S$ is a singular matrix\n- $det(S)=\\sqrt{3}$\n\n$$\nS=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & \\,0 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{3} & \\,\\,-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4 & \\,\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & \\,0 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{3} & \\,\\,-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4 & \\,\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\,\\,-1 \\\\ 4 & \\,\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\,-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & \\,-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(-{(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}+4)-2(-2\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{3})+0 \\\\  & =(-3+4)-2\\cdot (-\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =1+2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(S)=1+2\\sqrt{3}\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not ** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303357 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9405d7f-2eab-599d-9ba5-e87cacabdf95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303359} {:answer/id #uuid "8b70e71f-f769-57db-b7fb-a5767752d8e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303360} {:answer/id #uuid "916c7451-7165-5939-b18f-f24a87f57db6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303361} {:answer/id #uuid "8e92102a-d2be-58f6-bc96-f9d23e118a46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303362} {:answer/id #uuid "341dcfd3-2a7a-54a5-a51a-2cd79256e8e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "341dcfd3-2a7a-54a5-a51a-2cd79256e8e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303363} :answer-field/id #uuid "92720cbe-efa5-5123-a597-8ee071c3b10d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303358}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24cc52a8-4124-5277-acdf-def6004941a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-77478" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $R$ given below?\n\n- $R$ is a singular matrix\n- $det(R)=0$\n- $det(R)=1$\n\n \n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(R) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}|-\\frac{2}{5}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+\\frac{1}{5}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}(2-\\frac{3}{2})-\\frac{2}{5}(1-0)+\\frac{1}{5}(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot 1+\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}-\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{1}{10} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(R)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true."}]}
